From the calculation, near the atomization dish edge, radius is larger, the circumferential stress σ1 will far outweigh the radial stress σ2; When RPM is higher, the radius increased will dramatically increase σ1, which could lead to the edge crack of the atomization dish. So it is unfavorable to use the large radius of flat disk.
2. Structure analysis of the atomization
The shape structure of the atomization is shown in figure 5.
Atomizing device is composed of melting part, turning driving part and powder collecting part. Atomizing plate is fixed on the shaft of high speed motor directly and its shape is hemisphere-shaped to increase its strength and surface area and use the gravity of metal liquid sufficiently. A plate with fine threads is installed under the atomizing plate closely. The fine threads are fixed on the plate vertically which turns reversely driven by another high speed motor. The assembling position of the atomizing plate is in the middle of the plate with fine threads and doesn’t affect the respective turning. The metal liquid from crucible passing infusion tube onto atomizing plate is thrown off by eccentric force of high speed turning of the atomizing plate and pulverized to fine and small foggy metal liquid drips, meanwhile, the high-speeded turning fine threads lashing and impacting the fine and small foggy metal liquid drips to be pulverized before its solidifying to get the aim of atomizing foggy drips. Because the plate with fine threads and the atomizing plate turn reversely, the relative speed of foggy drips and fine threads is very high and its impacting atomizing effect is better. The impacting atomizing fine and small metal liquid drips solidify to fine metal powder and fall freely under the shell of atomizing device. The infusion tube is porcelain tube and its flow is controlled by control bar. The atomizing plate and plate with fine treads are driven by upper and lower motor directly without any other transmission, getting high efficiency, low energy consumption and credible running.
